// ============================================================================================
// MOH Trilogy Coop - PROTOTYPE B, "OPERATIONS BOARD".
//
// WHAT THIS IS.  A layout study for a denser main menu: the whole trilogy - 3 theatres,
// 12 missions, 52 maps - laid out as a wartime briefing board, on ONE screen, with a clear
// typographic hierarchy and no scrolling anywhere.  It is a PROTOTYPE.  It starts nothing,
// launches nothing, and writes only cvars whose names begin with coop_protoB.
//
// HOW TO OPEN IT.  Nothing under ui/proto/ is auto-loaded: the startup sweep is
// FS_ListFiles("ui/", "urc", qfalse, ...) at client/cl_ui.cpp:5634, and wantSubs=qfalse drops
// any path deeper than one level (qcommon/files.cpp:2426).  So, in the console:
//
//     exec ui/proto/coop_proto_b_open.cfg
//
// or by hand:
//
//     loadmenu proto/coop_proto_b_board
//     loadmenu proto/coop_proto_b_brief
//     pushmenu coop_proto_b_board
//
// pushmenu, never showmenu: UI_ShowMenu skips the focus call that turns the mouse on
// (cl_ui.cpp:5524 vs :5529).  BACK, bottom-left, is popmenu 0 and returns you to whatever was
// underneath - normally the real main menu, which this file never touches.
//
// fullscreen 0, NOT 1.  fullscreen only decides what happens to the 3D view: a fullscreen
// container hides it and calls Com_FakePause() when a server is running (cl_ui.cpp:1993-1996).
// A prototype opened mid-session should not pause a live coop server, and it costs nothing to
// avoid, because the shared chrome's `stretch both` ground is fully opaque - the world behind
// is covered anyway.  At the main menu the two are indistinguishable: pushmenu hides the menu
// underneath (uimenu.cpp:538) and the non-fullscreen branch clears the background.
//
// THE PAGING MECHANISM, and why there is no scrollbar.
// UIVertScroll registers no layout events of its own (uilib/uivertscroll.cpp:45-53) and has no
// item source; only ListBox/ListCtrl ever drive one.  A long list therefore cannot scroll - it
// has to be PAGED.  Three theatre tabs each drive one boolean, and every widget on a page
// carries an enabledcvar:
//     ALLIED ASSAULT   enabledcvar "!coop_protoBhide1"   visible while the cvar is 0 or unset
//     SPEARHEAD        enabledcvar "coop_protoBp2"
//     BREAKTHROUGH     enabledcvar "coop_protoBp3"
// The "!" form is uiwidget.cpp:1701 and already ships in ui/coop_loadout.urc:696.  Using it for
// page 1 means the board is correct with NO cvar registered at all - nothing has to be seeded
// before the menu opens, and UI_GetCvarInt uses Cvar_Find, so reading an absent cvar creates
// nothing (uilib/ui_init.cpp:57-64).  A gated-off widget returns early from Display
// (uiwidget.cpp:2027) AND is skipped by FindResponder (uiwidget.cpp:1736-1739), so a hidden
// page can neither draw nor eat a click from the page on top of it.
//
// GROUPING WITHOUT NESTING.  Widgets do not nest - every resource below is a flat, direct child
// of the menu container (uilib/uilayout.cpp:150).  Every "panel" here is therefore just a
// filled Widget declared BEFORE the things that sit on it: draw order is declaration order and
// hit-testing walks children last-to-first (uiwidget.cpp:1744), so a backing plate can never
// steal a click from the content drawn over it.  Grouping is done with position, a plate, and a
// brass header bar - there is no other kind of group available.
//
// THE THREE COLUMNS
//     x   8..140   ORDERS       the action rail: 6 primary, 4 reference
//     x 146..476   MISSION BOARD  3 theatre tabs, 6 mission blocks, up to 12 map chips each
//     x 482..632   DISPATCH     live readout of the chip you clicked, plus the board key
// y 0..70 and y 434..480 belong to ui/proto/coop_proto_chrome.inc (title plate, credit, BACK).
//
// CVARS THIS FILE READS OR WRITES - all proto-private, by design:
//     coop_protoBhide1 / coop_protoBp2 / coop_protoBp3   which theatre page is showing
//     coop_protoBsel                                     selected map id, shown in DISPATCH
//     coop_protoBshot                                    that map's loading art (linkcvartoshader)
//     coop_protoBord                                     last button pressed on the ORDERS rail
// It deliberately does NOT linkcvar a real game cvar.  ESC on any menu calls
// menuManager.PopMenu(qtrue) (cl_ui.cpp:3127), which runs Menu::RestoreCVars, which does a
// Cvar_Set on every widget cvarname - so a linkcvar pointed at a cvar that was not registered
// when the menu was pushed would CREATE it as an empty string, permanently defeating the engine
// default.  That is the bug-1669 failure mode arriving through the UI instead of through a
// script getcvar.  Read-only game state stays static text until something registers it first.
//
// FONTS are only the three this mod actually ships menus in: facfont-20, verdana-12,
// courier-16.  A font name the renderer cannot load is Com_Error(ERR_DROP) at
// uilib/uifont.cpp:299 - the client drops at menu load.  Every string below was measured
// against its rect using the real .RitualFont metric tables before it was written.
//
// ART is retail-only: menu_button_trans + textures/mohmenu/m_buttonhighlight (the exact hover
// idiom already shipped at ui/multiplayerstart.urc:174-175) and textures/mohmenu/dmloading/*
// for the map previews.  No new shader name is declared, so the bug-922 bare-name trap cannot
// fire.  Five maps ship no loading art (m6l3e, e3l1-e3l4); their chips are dimmed and DISPATCH
// says so, rather than silently leaving the previous map's picture up.
//
// borderstyle is spelled out on every widget: the default is border_indent, not none
// (uiwidget.cpp:747), and "RAISED" - used 40 times elsewhere in this mod's UI - is not a
// recognised value (uiwidget.cpp:1349-1360) and silently leaves the indent border drawn.
// textalign is written as centerx / centery / left / top: "center" and "xcenter" are NOT
// recognised (uiwidget.cpp:1511-1530), and the handler only ever reads argument 1, so each
// alignment needs its own line.
//
// Generated, then checked: every rect is inside the 640x480 canvas and inside the chrome's
// content contract, and every title fits its rect at its font's real metrics.
// ============================================================================================
menu "coop_proto_b_board" 640 480 NONE 0
bgcolor 0 0 0 1
borderstyle NONE
bgfill 0 0 0 1
fullscreen 0
virtualres 1
include "ui/proto/coop_proto_chrome.inc"

// ---- title, hard-coded, drawn over the chrome's cvar-driven pair ----------
